MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_001: Wow! You're really good with a bow, Petey.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_002: Hehe. You think so? Thanks for saying that.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_003: Hmhm! Need a training buddy? I'd be happy to\njoin you.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_004: Sure, but let's take a quick break first. I've worked up\nan appetite.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_005: Ooh, are those ginji fruits? Mind if I steal one\nfrom you?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_006: Of course. Take as much as you want.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_007: Well, if you say so. *chomp* Mmm!
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_008: Sofia...are you gonna scarf down the whole bag?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_009: Huh? Oh, um... Sorry? I guess I got carried away.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_010: Hehe... Seems like you were hungry!
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_011: Well, I am...or I was. But honestly, I just love food.\nWhat can I say? I'm a big eater.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_012: I've always been like this. It made me a bit unpopular\nback in my village.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_013: That's how I started working in a temple. Just\nwanted to make things easier on my parents.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_014: I mean, because of me, my brother was always\ngetting scraps. It wasn't an ideal situation.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_015: I get it. I have little brothers too, so I can understand\nhow you'd want to make things easier for him.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_016: I guess your brother gets to eat until his belly's full\nnow, right?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_017: I hope so, but...I haven't seen him in a while. Last\nI heard he was in some trouble.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_018: He left our mom and joined a group of bandits in\nthe mountains.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_019: Bandits? But why?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_020: No idea. And he was the kind of kid that could\nnever even kill a spider.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_021: Hey, Petey! Would you and your impressive bow\nskills be willing to do me a favor?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_022: Let's go find my brother and knock some sense into\nhim. It's bound to work if you're there.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_023: J-just stroll right into the bandits' lair? That's crazy!\nAnd scary! And dangerous!
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_024: Not with your amazing talent. You and me?\nWe could handle it, no problem. Please?!
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_025: Aww... I understand you're worried about your\nbrother, and I really can't say no.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_026: Alright. I'm on board. We'll get this done, Sofia.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_C_027: Yes! Thank you! Well, time's a-wastin'. Let's start\ntraining for our big mission.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_001: Thanks for everything you did the other day, Petey.\nWe definitely taught my brother a lesson.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_002: I'm glad we got him out of trouble, but I wasn't\nmuch help.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_003: What do you mean? You were the one who talked all\nthat sense into him!
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_004: "Don't make your big sis sad! She worries about you\nall the time."
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_005: "A sister like that is a precious thing." I really think\nhe got the message.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_006: I just told him what I'd tell my own brothers if they\nwere in trouble.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_007: I'm sure he could tell. That's probably what made all\nthe difference.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_008: But I was only able to persuade him because you\nwere there.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_009: That's not true at all. I couldn't get through, even\nwhen he was tied up and forced to listen.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_010: But you got your feelings across to him. I know\nyou did.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_011: Then why was he being so defiant?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_012: Maybe he was sad about all the trouble he's caused,\nbut he didn't know how to apologize.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_013: One of my brothers is like that. He gets all furious\nand then blurts out, "I'm trying to say I'm sorry!"
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_014: Really? I guess that could explain it. Anyway, thanks\nfor everything, Petey.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_015: Our brother and sister bonds are what did the trick.\nHow's he been doing since all this happened?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_016: Well, after everything he's done, I can't really call\nhim my sweet little brother anymore.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_017: But he said once he's paid for his crimes, he'll head\nback to the village, work hard, and look after Mom.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_018: I hope he'll be able to live a decent life, but I still\nworry about him.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_019: I just wish I had the ability to send a little gold back\nto my family every now and then.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_020: Oh? Temple salaries aren't all that bad, are they?
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_021: No, they're not. I just usually blow most of my money\non food.
MID_SE_Pet_Sop_B_022: Heh... And onward goes the battle.